title: The Economic Crisis
new-page: true
is-card: true
view-if: crisis_urgency >= 1 and crisis_program_timer = 0 and economic_plan = 0 and recession_seen == 1
frequency: 200
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; crisis_program_timer = 5
card-image: img/bankrun.jpg
tags: party_affairs, govt_affairs

= Addressing the Economic Crisis

The party is divided over how to answer the recession.

Netzwerk Berlin argues that the debt brake and the trust of the markets come first: the crisis will pass, and a spending spree would only bring back inflation.

The AfA and the DGB want a large public investment programme, the "Zukunftsprogramm": rail, power grids, schools and housing, paid for with new borrowing. Its critics say it would break the debt brake and overheat prices.

The Parlamentarische Linke says that investment alone leaves the real problem untouched. When steelworks and car suppliers close, the state should take stakes in them and run them with their workers, as part of a social and ecological transformation of industry.

The Seeheimer Kreis proposes a smaller plan: longer short-time work, tax credits for companies that invest, and targeted job programmes in the regions worst hit, all within the debt brake. The AfA calls it far too small.

- @support_centrist: Support Netzwerk Berlin.
- @support_labor: Support the AfA.
- @support_left: Support the Parlamentarische Linke.
- @support_moderate: Support the Seeheimer Kreis.
- @defer: Defer making a decision until we have more information.
- @easy_discard

@support_centrist
subtitle: Hold the line on the budget and let the crisis pass.
on-arrival: center_strength += 5; center_dissent -= 5; labor_dissent += 10; investment_support -= 1; left_dissent += 10;

The unions are furious. People are losing their jobs, and the SPD is talking about the debt brake? Netzwerk Berlin replies that empty promises are worse than none.

For now, our line is that the crisis must run its course.

@support_labor
subtitle: Call for a large public investment programme.
on-arrival: center_dissent += 10; left_dissent += 5; labor_strength += 5; investment_support += 1;
go-to: plan_adopted if investment_support >= 3; plan_support if investment_support < 3

@plan_support

Our support for the Zukunftsprogramm wins applause from the unions and many economists, but Netzwerk Berlin warns about the debt brake, and the left says that it leaves the ownership of industry untouched.

We have not yet convinced the party to adopt the plan. More work needs to be done.

@plan_adopted
on-arrival: investment_adopted = 1; labor_dissent -= 15; reformist_dissent -= 10; labor_strength += 10; center_strength -= 10; center_dissent += 20; left_dissent += 5; economic_plan = 1

The party formally adopts the Zukunftsprogramm! [? if spd_in_government == 1 : We can begin to put it into practice as soon as we hold the economics or finance ministry. ?][? if spd_in_government = 0 : It will be the centre of our next campaign. ?]

@support_left
subtitle: Call for public ownership and the transformation of industry.
on-arrival: left_strength += 10; reformist_dissent += 5; labor_dissent += 5; nationalization_support += 2
go-to: support_left_progress if nationalization_support < 3; adopt_left if nationalization_support >= 3

@support_left_progress

We argue that the state should take stakes in the plants that are closing. The left says that this is what democratic socialism means, while the Seeheimer and some trade unionists say that it is unrealistic and would scare off every investor.

We have not yet adopted the plan. More work needs to be done.

@adopt_left
on-arrival: left_strength += 15; left_dissent -= 10; reformist_dissent += 10; labor_dissent += 6; nationalization_adopted = 1; firewall_erosion += 1; economic_plan = 3; linke_relation += 5*(1-dissent)

The party adopts the plan for the transformation of industry! [? if spd_in_government == 1 : We can begin as soon as we hold the economics or finance ministry. ?] The business associations will fight it hard. [? if spd_in_government == 0 : It will be hard to carry out from opposition. ?]

@support_moderate
subtitle: Call for a targeted plan within the debt brake.
on-arrival: moderate_plan_support += 1; reformist_strength += 8; reformist_dissent -= 5; left_dissent += 6; labor_dissent += 5
go-to: adopt_moderate if moderate_plan_support >= 2; support_moderate_progress if moderate_plan_support < 2

@support_moderate_progress

The Seeheimer say that their plan is the only one the Union and the FDP could accept. The AfA and the left call it a drop in the ocean.

We have not yet adopted the plan. More work needs to be done.

@adopt_moderate
on-arrival: reformist_strength += 10; reformist_dissent -= 10; left_dissent += 8; labor_dissent += 6; moderate_plan_adopted = 1; economic_plan = 2; coalition_dissent -= 1 if unemployment_rate > 8; cdu_relation += 5;

The party adopts the targeted jobs plan! [? if spd_in_government == 1 : We can begin as soon as we hold the economics or finance ministry. ?]

@defer

We hold off on a decision and wait for more figures. The unions say that doing nothing is also a decision.
